# Mapping Blood Pressure OBX Segments to FHIR R4 Observation

## The Core Challenge

In HL7 v2, blood pressure is typically represented as **two separate OBX segments** (one for systolic, one for diastolic), while FHIR R4 models it as a **single Observation resource with `component` elements**.

---

## HL7 v2 Source Structure

```
OBX|1|NM|8480-6^Systolic Blood Pressure^LN||119||mm[Hg]|...
OBX|2|NM|8462-4^Diastolic Blood Pressure^LN||84||mm[Hg]|...
```

---

## FHIR R4 Target Structure

Based on **Evidence [1]** (LOINC `55284-4`, Blood Pressure, value type: `component`), the mapped resource looks like:

```json
{
  "resourceType": "Observation",
  "status": "final",
  "category": [{
    "coding": [{
      "system": "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/observation-category",
      "code": "vital-signs"
    }]
  }],
  "code": {
    "coding": [{
      "system": "http://loinc.org",
      "code": "55284-4",
      "display": "Blood Pressure"
    }]
  },
  "effectiveDateTime": "2010-03-01T06:22:41-05:00",
  "component": [
    {
      "code": {
        "coding": [{
          "system": "http://loinc.org",
          "code": "8480-6",
          "display": "Systolic Blood Pressure"
        }]
      },
      "valueQuantity": {
        "value": 119.11,
        "unit": "mm[Hg]",
        "system": "http://unitsofmeasure.org",
        "code": "mm[Hg]"
      }
    },
    {
      "code": {
        "coding": [{
          "system": "http://loinc.org",
          "code": "8462-4",
          "display": "Diastolic Blood Pressure"
        }]
      },
      "valueQuantity": {
        "value": 84.52,
        "unit": "mm[Hg]",
        "system": "http://unitsofmeasure.org",
        "code": "mm[Hg]"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

---

## Key Mapping Rules

| HL7 v2 Field | FHIR R4 Target | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| OBX-3 (panel code) | `Observation.code` | Use **`55284-4`** as the panel LOINC |
| OBX-3 (systolic) `8480-6` | `component[0].code` | Per Evidence [1] systolic component |
| OBX-3 (diastolic) `8462-4` | `component[1].code` | Per Evidence [1] diastolic component |
| OBX-5 (numeric value) | `component[x].valueQuantity.value` | Evidence [1]: `119.11` / `84.52` |
| OBX-6 (units) `mm[Hg]` | `component[x].valueQuantity.unit` | UCUM code `mm[Hg]` |
| OBX-11 (result status `F`) | `Observation.status` = `"final"` | Per Evidence [1] |
| OBX-14 (observation time) | `Observation.effectiveDateTime` | Per Evidence [1] |
| — | `category` = `vital-signs` | Required for BP per Evidence [1] |

---

## Critical Design Decisions

1. **Group into ONE Observation**: Two v2 OBX segments → one FHIR Observation. The `component` value type (Evidence [1]) is the distinguishing pattern vs. standalone observations like hemoglobin (Evidence [2], `valueQuantity`).

2. **Panel LOINC `55284-4`** goes on `Observation.code`; component-specific LOINCs (`8480-6`, `8462-4`) go inside each `component.code`.

3. **No top-level `valueQuantity`**: Unlike sodium (Evidence [3]) or BMI (Evidence [4]) which use `valueQuantity` directly, blood pressure uses **only** `component` elements — `Observation.value[x]` is intentionally absent.

4. **UCUM units**: `mm[Hg]` maps to `http://unitsofmeasure.org` system.
